  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230697/assets/063c18aee27eba87852117748b3f90bf75a9785b466516cbf88c01f4300f94e9.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "The polyhedron is a **pentagonal prism** since it has two identical pentagonal faces connected by equal parallel line segments.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a pyramid since a pyramid must have triangular faces (except, possibly, for the base) that meet at a single point.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube.",
